<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/7th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Tertry</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">687</span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Tertry was fought in 687 near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peronne">Péronne</a> in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pippin-of-herstal">Pippin of Herstal</a>, mayor of the palace of Austrasia, and the Neustrian mayor Berchar with King Theuderic III. Pippin's victory made him master of all the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frankish-kingdom">Frankish kingdoms</a> and secured his family's dominance, which led eventually to the Carolingian monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-tertry.jpg" alt="Battle of Tertry" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jean-Michel Moreau · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jean_Michel_Moreau_-_Pepin_of_Herstal_after_the_battle_of_Tertry_in_687.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
